      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:6:5:3",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ السُّحْتِ فَقَالَ هُوَ الرِّشَا فِي الْحُكْمِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Sinan, from Ibn Muskam, from Yazeed Bin Farqad who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about ‘السُّحْتِ’ (forbidden earnings). So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The bribery in the judgement’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Sinan from ibn Muskan from Yazid ibn Farqad who has narrated the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about al-Suht (sinful earning). He (the Imam) said, ‘It is accepting a bribe to issue judgments.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
